.Dd November 2, 2026
.Dt SHELLCHECK 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm shellcheck
.Nd find errors in shell scripts
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar options
.Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads shell scripts and reports syntax errors, common mistakes and
portability problems without executing them.
.Fl s Ar shell
chooses the shell dialect;
.Fl x
follows sourced files;
.Fl f Ar format
chooses the output format, such as tty, gcc or json.
A file named
.Ql -
is read from standard input.
.Ql shellcheck --help
describes the other options.
.Pp
The x86-64 GNU root installs the project's static Linux build, version
0.11.0, under
.Pa /opt/shellcheck
when built with
.Ql GNU_AGENTS=shellcheck
or
.Ql GNU_AGENTS=all .
.Pa /usr/bin/shellcheck
and
.Pa /bin/shellcheck
link to it.
The GPL version 3 or later is in
.Pa /opt/shellcheck/LICENSE .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa .shellcheckrc
settings read from the script's directory or a parent
.It Pa ~/.shellcheckrc
user settings when no nearer file is found
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 for no findings, 1 for findings, 2 when a file could not be processed,
3 for a bad invocation, and 4 for a bad option.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ shellcheck -s sh script.sh
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sh 1
.Pp
.Lk https://www.shellcheck.net/wiki/ "The ShellCheck diagnostics"
